                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_407">Norwich, Norfolk.
                        Dominican convent</orgName><p>'Memorandum quod venerabilis domina Domina
                        Johanna de Clyffton quondam uxor domini Johannis Clyffton militis de
                        Bokenhamcastell, quorum animabus deus propicietur, per procurationem ff. J.
                        Gillyngham, istud Psalterum preciosum contulit conventui ordinis fratrum
                        predicatorum Norwic', que obiit anno domini millesimo quadringentesimo
                        quinquagesimo quintodecimo die mensis Novembris' (fol. 1v) (reproduced in
                        Sotheby's catalogue, 1988, p. 25).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Made for Elizabeth Badlesmere (1313--1356),
                     wife of Sir Edmund Mortimer (d. 1331) and later of William de Bohun (d. 1360),
                     first earl of Northampton. Lady Joan Clifton (d. 1450); given by her to the
                     Norwich Dominicans.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John Jacob Astor III (1822--1890) and
                     descended in the family: the manuscript was first noted in the Supplement as
                     belonging to Lord Astor (Wantage, Oxon.). </provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sold by the Astors at Sotheby's. 21 June
                     1988, lot 52 (see sale catalogue, with colour and b&amp;w reproductions);
                     bought by Quaritch for £1,400,000 on behalf of Ladislaus von Hoffmann (d.
                     2014), Washington, D.C.; offered at Christie's, 7 July 2010, lot 30, with
                     colour plates (unsold and returned to owner).</provenance>
               </history>
